{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerNonneg","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerNonneg","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobMonotonicity"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerNonneg.blochWigner_lob_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerNonneg.blochWigner_lob_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerNonneg.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**`0 ≤ D(z)` for every `z` in the upper half plane.**\n\nThe general nonnegativity that `ManifoldVolumeBridge` declined to assume as a class\nfield.  Note this is the **non-strict** statement — see the module header for why\nstrictness does not follow from the same argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerNonneg.volume_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerNonneg.volume_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochWignerNonneg.lean#L57-L64","doc":"**An ideal tetrahedron has nonnegative volume.**\n\nMilnor's formula plus the fact that the three dihedral angles are positive and sum to\n`π`, which is exactly the hypothesis of `lob_sum_nonneg`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}